content.text:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
## 1. Primary Request and Intent

The user made a sequence of requests about the Lobu Memory schema-graph page (`/buremba/memory`) and one about the Connectors page:

1. **Diagnose and fix schema-graph legibility.** User showed a screenshot of an ERD with colliding edge labels and a truncated node name ("Comp…"), asking: *"what's the best in class solution for these? i want default view to be clean for people, no matter how many edges are, how long their name is etc."*

2. **Implement the fix and verify against prod.** *"let's do the fix, boot forntend only on prod backend pi so we can confirm it's working"* — frontend-only vite proxying to the real prod backend.

3. **Move authoring into the side panel.** *"add relationship and create entity type, instead of seperate page or dialog, could we use the side panel for it?"*

4. **Make the create button primary.** *"create entity type button can be primary no?"*

5. **Put BOTH edit and create entity type in the panel (reversing my recommendation), and remove the Needs setup chip.** *"why don't we put the edit entitty type and create entity type in there instead of a seperate page? also no need to put needs setup chip here, we already show the needs setup at first anyways."*

6. **Two open design questions.** *"do you think the sidebar here should be expandable? also in mobile how will it be"*

7. **Bug report.** *"create entity type button in mobile doesn't work"* — confirmed a regression I had introduced.

## 2. Key Technical Concepts

- **React Flow / @xyflow/react v12** — custom node types, custom edge types, `BaseEdge`, `EdgeLabelRenderer`, `getSmoothStepPath`, `fitViewOptions.nodes`, `onNodeMouseEnter`/`onEdgeMouseEnter`, `useNodesState`
- **ELK.js layered layout** — `elk.algorithm: layered`, `elk.edgeRouting: ORTHOGONAL`, edge-edge/node-node spacing options; ELK's `laidOut.edges[].sections[].bendPoints` are computed but **discarded** (only `laidOut.children` is read) — this is the un-addressed Tier 3 structural issue
- **Best-in-class ERD patterns** — Azimutt, ChartDB, drawDB, Supabase schema visualizer, Neo4j Bloom: edge text stays OFF the resting canvas; one line per node pair; progressive disclosure over better layout
- **Union-find clustering** (`schemaClusters`) for connected components
- **React context** for canvas→panel callbacks (avoids polluting React Flow node `data`, which is value-compared in `renderedStateOf`)
- **Tailwind responsive breakpoints** (`lg:`) and the `hidden lg:flex` trap
- **Bun workspace / git worktrees** — `make task-setup NAME=<slug>`, submodule `packages/owletto`
- **agent-browser CLI** for authenticated browser verification; `set viewport <w> <h>` (NOT `emulate viewport`)
- **better-auth cookie signing** — HMAC-SHA256, base64 (not base64url), URL-encoded; `__Secure-better-auth.session_token`
- **Vite `LOBU_API_PROXY`** — same-origin proxy for `/api`, `/oauth`, `/connect` with Set-Cookie rewriting

## 3. Files and Code Sections

### Worktree A: `.claude/worktrees/schema-graph-legibility` (branch `feat/schema-graph-legibility`)

#### `packages/owletto/src/components/entities/entity-schema-graph.ts` (MODIFIED, +160)
Pure model + ELK layout module; unit-testable, React-free. Central to the legibility fix.

Edge bundling — pair key changed from per-relationship-type to per-ordered-pair:
```ts
/** One declared relationship type inside a bundled edge. */
export interface SchemaEdgeRelationship {
	slug: string;
	label: string;
	isSymmetric: boolean;
	ruleCount: number;
}

interface SchemaEdgeData {
	relationships: SchemaEdgeRelationship[];
	/** Only true when EVERY bundled relationship is symmetric. */
	isSymmetric: boolean;
}
```
```ts
const byPair = new Map<string, SchemaGraphEdge>();
const byPairAndType = new Map<string, SchemaEdgeRelationship>();

const typeKey = `${rt.slug}|${source}|${target}`;
const counted = byPairAndType.get(typeKey);
if (counted) { counted.ruleCount += 1; continue; }

const pairKey = `${source}|${target}`;
const bundled = byPair.get(pairKey);
if (bundled) {
    bundled.data.relationships.push(relationship);
    bundled.data.isSymmetric = bundled.data.isSymmetric && rt.is_symmetric;
    continue;
}
const edge: SchemaGraphEdge = {
    id: `pair:${source}|${target}`,   // `|` cannot occur in a slug
    source, target,
    data: { relationships: [relationship], isSymmetric: rt.is_symmetric },
};
```

Node sizing — replaced `const NODE_WIDTH = 220; const HEADER_HEIGHT = 44;`:
```ts
const NODE_MIN_WIDTH = 200;
const NODE_MAX_WIDTH = 320;
const HEADER_HEIGHT = 56;   // two lines
const TITLE_CHAR_WIDTH = 7.4;   // 13px / 600 weight
const META_CHAR_WIDTH = 5.9;    // 11px / 400 weight
const TITLE_CHROME_WIDTH = 84;
const META_CHROME_WIDTH = 48;

function nodeWidth(label: string, metaLabel: string): number {
	return Math.round(Math.min(NODE_MAX_WIDTH, Math.max(
		NODE_MIN_WIDTH,
		TITLE_CHROME_WIDTH + label.length * TITLE_CHAR_WIDTH,
		META_CHROME_WIDTH + metaLabel.length * META_CHAR_WIDTH,
	)));
}

function schemaMetaLabel(fieldCount: number, entityCount: number | undefined): string {
	const parts: string[] = [];
	if (fieldCount > 0) parts.push(`${fieldCount} ${fieldCount === 1 ? "field" : "fields"}`);
	if (typeof entityCount === "number")
		parts.push(`${entityCount.toLocaleString()} ${entityCount === 1 ? "record" : "records"}`);
	return parts.join(" · ");
}
```
