BODY = f"""
<div class="wrap">
<header>
  <div class="eyebrow">lobu-ai/owletto &middot; feat/schema-graph-legibility</div>
  <h1>Making the Memory schema map readable at any size</h1>
  <p class="lede">Captured against the real <span class="m">app.lobu.ai</span> backend on the <span class="m">buremba</span> workspace &mdash; 14 entity types, 3 relationship pairs. Before shots come from an unmodified <span class="m">origin/main</span> checkout running beside the branch.</p>
</header>

<section>
  <h2>The map itself</h2>
  <ul class="findings">
    <li><b>Labels collided.</b> Six paths between three boxes each carried a name, stacked on top of one another &mdash; &ldquo;Clai Proposes Merge With&rdquo; is two labels overlapping, not a typo.</li>
    <li><b>Names truncated.</b> Every box was a fixed 220px with the name and the counts sharing one row, so the name was the only flexible item &mdash; <span class="m">Company</span> rendered as <span class="m">Comp&hellip;</span>.</li>
    <li><b>Islands crowded out the schema.</b> Unconnected types took the left half of the canvas and pushed the actual diagram into a corner.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="pair">
    <div class="shot"><span class="tag b">Before</span>{img("before-memory","Schema map before: overlapping edge labels, truncated Company name, island column dominating the canvas")}</div>
    <div class="shot"><span class="tag a">After</span>{img("after-memory","Schema map after: three bundled edges with count pills, full type names on two lines, diagram framed on the connected subgraph")}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="note"><b>What changed.</b> Relationships between the same pair bundle onto one path, so six paths become three. Names leave the resting canvas entirely &mdash; a bundled path shows a count pill (<span class="m">2</span>, <span class="m">3</span>) and reveals its names on hover, on tap, or through <code>aria-label</code>. Each box is sized from its own measured title and meta text, clamped 200&ndash;320px, with the name on its own line. <code>fitView</code> frames only the connected subgraph.</div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Authoring moved beside the map</h2>
  <ul class="findings">
    <li>The relationship form was a modal that <b>covered the very boxes you pick between</b> &mdash; its two inputs are From and To.</li>
    <li>Editing a type navigated away to <span class="m">/$owner/entity-types/$slug</span>, hiding the map being edited.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="shot"><span class="tag a">After &middot; type editor in the panel</span>{img("after-editor","Company type editor rendered in the side panel at 440px with the schema map still visible")}</div>
  <div class="note">The panel widens to 440px for the editor and hands the space back on close. Company&rsquo;s 18-field editor fits without horizontal overflow (<span class="m">scrollWidth 440 === clientWidth 440</span>).</div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>The divider drags</h2>
  <div class="shot"><span class="tag a">After &middot; dragged wider</span>{img("after-resized","Schema panel dragged wider, canvas correspondingly narrower")}</div>
  <div class="scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Gesture</th><th>Panel</th><th>Canvas</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Rest (index)</td><td class="n">288</td><td class="n">799</td><td>Mode default</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Drag left 150px</td><td class="n">438</td><td class="n">649</td><td>Follows the pointer</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Reload</td><td class="n">438</td><td class="n">649</td><td>Restored from storage</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Drag past the window edge</td><td class="n">720</td><td class="n">367</td><td>Stops at the ceiling</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Same, in a 1060px window</td><td class="n">387</td><td class="n">320</td><td>Canvas keeps its floor</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Double-click</td><td class="n">288</td><td class="n">799</td><td>Override cleared</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Open editor after dragging to 600</td><td class="n">600</td><td class="n">&mdash;</td><td>Drag beats the default</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <div class="note"><b>Hand-rolled, no new dependency.</b> <span class="m">react-resizable-panels</span> would bring a layout engine to a problem that is <code>startWidth - dx</code> clamped. Arrow keys nudge 16px and Home resets, since the panel hosts the type editor and a pointer-only divider would put that behind a mouse.</div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Narrow viewports</h2>
  <p class="lede">There is no room for canvas and editor at 390px, so the editor takes the screen &mdash; the same trade the routed page made, minus the navigation. The divider is hidden below <span class="m">lg</span>: with nothing beside the panel, there is no split to tune.</p>
  <div class="shot narrow"><span class="tag a">After &middot; 390&times;844</span>{img("after-mobile","Type editor full-bleed on a 390px viewport with the canvas yielded")}</div>
  <div class="note">This is also a <b>bug fix</b>: the panel was <code>hidden lg:flex</code>, so below that breakpoint &ldquo;Create entity type&rdquo; set a mode nothing rendered and the button looked dead. A dragged desktop width does not leak here &mdash; the width rides a CSS variable behind a <span class="m">lg:</span> prefix.</div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Connectors: one redundant chip</h2>
  <p class="lede">The list already sorts needs-setup connectors first and badges each card, so the filter chip only restated what was already on screen. Eight filters remain.</p>
  <div class="pair">
    <div class="shot"><span class="tag b">Before</span>{img("before-connectors","Connectors filter row including a Needs setup chip")}</div>
    <div class="shot"><span class="tag a">After</span>{img("after-connectors","Connectors filter row with the Needs setup chip removed")}</div>
  </div>
</section>

<footer>Verified against the production backend via an authenticated browser session. No form in these captures was submitted &mdash; the save path is unproven and called out in the PR.</footer>
</div>
"""

open("schema-graph-comparison.html","w").write(HEAD + BODY)
print("written", len(HEAD+BODY)//1024, "KB")
